---
description: Rich table widget — columns, grouping, pivot, filtering, formatting, visualization, layout
globs: dashboards/**/*.yaml
alwaysApply: false
---

<rule>
<meta>
  This rule covers the `rich_table` widget: columns, image/video values, grouping, pivot, filtering, sorting, conditional formatting, data presets, actions, export, and visualization.
  Activate when creating or editing rich_table widgets in dashboard YAML.
</meta>

<schema>
  <rich_table_widget>
    ```yaml
    - id: my_table
      type: rich_table
      col_span: 15                          # >12 for wide tables with horizontal scroll
      datasource: total_by_ad              # Key, projection name, or inline { sql }
      title: My Table                       # Optional
      columns: []                           # Required. Column definitions
      column_order: [col1, col2]            # Optional. Display order
      grouping: {}                          # Optional
      pivot: {}                             # Optional
      filtering: {}                         # Optional
      sorting: {}                           # Optional
      totals: {}                            # Optional. Grand total row
      selectable: true                      # Optional. Row selection
      highlight: {}                         # Optional. Cross-highlight
      export: {}                            # Optional
      conditional_formatting: []            # Optional
      visualization: {}                     # Optional
      layout: {}                            # Optional. Presets and responsive
      data_presets: {}                      # Optional. Projection-first presets
      actions: {}                           # Optional. Row actions
    ```
  </rich_table_widget>
</schema>

<options>
  <column_types>
    Three column types (discriminated union on `type`):

    | Type | Purpose | Extra fields |
    |---|---|---|
    | `dimension` | Categorical/text | (base fields only) |
    | `metric` | Aggregated numeric | `aggregate: sum \| avg \| count \| min \| max` |
    | `calculated` | Expression-based | `expression: "SQL expression"` |
  </column_types>

  <column_base_fields>
    ```yaml
    - id: language                          # Required
      label: Lang                           # Optional
      type: dimension                       # Required
      width: { type: fixed, value: 60 }    # Optional. Number or { type, value, min, max }
      pinned: left                          # Optional. left | right
      truncate: true                        # Optional
      hidden: false                         # Optional. Hide column
      auto_hide: true                        # Optional. Auto-hide when 100% null
      mapping: { id: languages }            # Optional. Value mapping ref
      normalize: capitalize                 # Optional. capitalize | uppercase | lowercase
      format: {}                            # Optional. Number formatting
      editable: true                        # Optional. Inline editing
      skill: update_budget                  # Optional. Write skill on save
      description: "..."                    # Optional. Header tooltip (also ai_hint fallback)
      ai_hint: "..."                        # Optional. AI context
      tooltip: {}                           # Optional. Programmable tooltip
      render: {}                            # Optional. Image/video renderer (dimension) or stacked cell (any column)
      overflow:                             # Optional
        strategy: truncate                  #   truncate | wrap | expand
        tooltip: { enabled: true, maxWidth: 420 }
    ```
  </column_base_fields>

  <column_format>
    ```yaml
    format:
      type: number | currency | percent | timestamp | trend
      decimals: 2                           # Optional. Auto-detected from data when omitted
      prefix: "$"                           # Optional
      suffix: "%"                           # Optional
      locale: "en-US"                       # Optional. BCP 47 locale tag
      abbreviate_above: 1000               # Optional. Min value to abbreviate
      pattern: "yyyy-MM-dd HH:mm"          # Optional. Timestamp format pattern
    ```

    **Adaptive decimals:** When `decimals` is not set, the system automatically detects
    the optimal precision from the data using DuckDB column profiling. This provides
    Excel-like adaptive formatting — integers display as integers, decimals show the
    minimum precision needed to represent all values accurately (up to 6 digits).

    **5 format types:**
    | Type | Description |
    |---|---|
    | `number` | Numeric with locale formatting |
    | `currency` | Currency with $ prefix |
    | `percent` | Percentage (×100 + %) |
    | `timestamp` | Date/time with optional `pattern` |
    | `trend` | Trend indicator (up/down arrows) |
  </column_format>

  <column_width>
    ```yaml
    # Simple fixed width
    width: 120

    # Detailed config
    width:
      type: fixed | flex | auto
      value: 120                            # fixed: pixels, flex: weight
      min: 80                               # Optional. Min px
      max: 400                              # Optional. Max px
    ```
  </column_width>

  <image_values>
    Image cells are configured through `render.type: image` on `dimension` columns only.
    Skipper proxies, resizes, and caches image variants through `/api/media/image`; do not put raw remote image URLs into HTML/markdown to bypass this.

    ```yaml
    columns:
      - id: creative_name
        label: Creative
        type: dimension

      - id: creative_image
        label: Image
        type: dimension
        width: { type: fixed, value: 132 }
        render:
          type: image
          src_column: creative_image        # Optional. Defaults to this column id
          alt_column: creative_name         # Optional. May reference hidden columns
          fit: cover                        # cover | contain
          placeholder: blur                 # blur | none
          zoom: true                        # Click/Enter opens preview dialog
          local_dir: media                  # local:// resolves inside dashboard/tab media/
          allowed_domains:
            - appewa.com
            - "*.appewa.com"
            - e2w2a.pro
    ```

    Supported source values:
    - `https://...` — allowed domains only; route applies SSRF guards and resize/cache.
    - `blob://root/key` — preferred for generated/synced assets, same BlobAdapter path used by notebook `.data/*.parquet`.
    - `local://file.webp` — filesystem roots only, inside `local_dir` (default `media`).

    Validation rules:
    - `src_column` and `alt_column` must reference declared widget columns; use `hidden: true` for helper columns.
    - `allowed_domains` entries are hostnames or leading wildcard patterns like `*.appewa.com`; no scheme/path/port.
    - `local_dir` is relative and cannot contain `.` or `..` path segments.
  </image_values>

  <video_values>
    Video cells are configured through `render.type: video` on `dimension` columns only.
    Skipper serves video bytes through `/api/media/video` with dashboard READ auth, source allowlists, SSRF guards, and byte-range support. The UI uses the browser's native `<video controls>` player; do not add custom player config to YAML.

    ```yaml
    columns:
      - id: creative_name
        label: Creative
        type: dimension

      - id: creative_video
        label: Video
        type: dimension
        width: { type: fixed, value: 220 }
        render:
          type: video
          src_column: video_uri             # Optional. Defaults to this column id
          title_column: creative_name       # Optional. Accessible player label
          poster_column: poster_uri         # Optional. Image poster; may reference hidden columns
          fit: contain                      # cover | contain
          preload: metadata                 # none | metadata | auto
          local_dir: media                  # local:// resolves inside dashboard/tab media/
          allowed_domains:
            - appewa.com
            - "*.appewa.com"
            - e2w2a.pro
    ```

    Supported source values:
    - `https://...` — allowed domains only; route applies SSRF guards and supports Range requests.
    - `blob://root/key` — preferred for generated/synced assets, same BlobAdapter path used by notebook `.data/*.parquet`.
    - `local://file.mp4` — filesystem roots only, inside `local_dir` (default `media`).

    Supported video extensions: `.mp4`, `.m4v`, `.mov`, `.ogv`, `.webm`.
    Supported poster extensions: `.png`, `.jpg`, `.jpeg`, `.webp`, `.gif`.

    Validation rules:
    - `src_column`, `title_column`, and `poster_column` must reference declared widget columns; use `hidden: true` for helper URI/title columns.
    - `allowed_domains` entries are hostnames or leading wildcard patterns like `*.appewa.com`; no scheme/path/port.
    - `local_dir` is relative and cannot contain `.` or `..` path segments.
    - Use `preload: none` for dense tables with many videos; use `metadata` when seek/duration readiness matters.
  </video_values>

  <stacked_values>
    Stacked cells compose 2-3 formatted values into a single cell via `render.type: stacked`. One data row stays one table row (no extra rows are inserted). Unlike image/video, stacked render is allowed on `dimension`, `metric`, and `calculated` columns.

    Each `line` references a declared column (usually `hidden: true`), picks a typographic `role`, and may carry an inline `indicator`.

    ```yaml
    columns:
      - id: spend
        type: metric
        aggregate: sum
        hidden: true
        format: { type: currency, decimals: 0 }
      - id: roas_delta
        type: metric
        aggregate: avg
        hidden: true
        format: { type: trend, decimals: 1, suffix: "%" }
      - id: delivery_status
        type: dimension
        hidden: true

      - id: performance
        label: Performance
        type: dimension
        width: { type: fixed, value: 220 }
        render:
          type: stacked
          gap: compact                       # compact | cozy  (vertical spacing)
          align: start                       # start | center | end
          lines:
            - { column: spend, role: primary }
            - { column: roas_delta, role: secondary, indicator: trend }
            - { column: delivery_status, role: tertiary, indicator: dot, mapping: { id: status_dot } }
    ```

    Roles: `primary` (headline, emphasized), `secondary` / `tertiary` (progressively muted, smaller).

    Line indicators:
    | Indicator | Renders |
    |---|---|
    | `trend` | Reuses `format.type: trend` — arrow (▲/▼/—) + sign + semantic color. Referenced column should use a `trend` format. |
    | `dot` | Semantic status dot; resolve the color token through the line `mapping` (e.g. `success`/`warning`/`destructive`/`neutral`). Exposes an accessible label. |
    | `badge` | Compact pill with the formatted value. |
    | `none` | Plain text (default). |

    Stacked cells are **display-only** — the column holds no data of its own. Point `sorting`, filtering, and `selection` at the underlying (usually `hidden: true`) columns, never at the stacked column id.

    Validation rules (hard errors — fail `a7s validate`):
    - `lines` must have 1-3 entries. The anatomy is fixed: `primary` / `secondary` / `tertiary`; there is no fourth tier.
    - Every `line.column` must reference a declared widget column.
    - A line cannot reference the stacked column itself, nor another `stacked` column (no nesting).
    - Per-line `format` overrides the referenced column's format; otherwise the referenced column's format/mapping is inherited.

    Validation warnings (non-fatal, but fix them):
    - Give stacked columns vertical room via `visualization.row_height`: **2 lines → `large`, 3 lines → `xlarge`** (the default density fits ~1 line). Too small a row height clips the cell.
    - `indicator: trend` should target a numeric column (a `metric`/`calculated` column, or a line/column with a numeric `format` such as `trend`/`currency`/`number`/`percent`). The arrow only renders for numeric values.
    - `indicator: dot` should provide a `mapping` (on the line or the referenced column) so the value resolves to a status token (`success`/`warning`/`destructive`/`neutral`). Without one the dot falls back to neutral.
  </stacked_values>

  <visualization_styles>
    | Style | Description |
    |---|---|
    | `default` | Standard table |
    | `minimal` | Clean, minimal borders |
    | `structured` | Grid-heavy structure |
    | `bloomberg` | Bloomberg terminal style |
    | `vercel` | Vercel dashboard style |
  </visualization_styles>

  <density_options>
    `compact` | `comfortable` | `spacious`
  </density_options>

  <row_heights>
    `small` | `medium` | `large` | `xlarge` | `2xlarge` | `3xlarge` | `4xlarge`

    Use `2xlarge` for compact thumbnails, `3xlarge` for inspection rows, and `4xlarge` for gallery-like image/video tables.
  </row_heights>

  <conditional_formatting_types>
    | Type | Description | Key fields |
    |---|---|---|
    | `color_scale` | Gradient colors | `palette`, `steps[]` or `steps: auto`, `value_sql?`, `apply_to: cell\|text` |
    | `icon_set` | Rule-based icons | `rules: [{ op, value, icon }]` |
    | `data_bar` | In-cell bars | `min?`, `max?`, `color?` |

    **Auto color scale:** Use `steps: auto` to automatically generate a 5-point gradient
    from data percentiles (min → P25 → P50 → P75 → max).

    **Palette options (design system):**
    - Diverging: `red_green` (default), `blue_orange`, `purple_teal`, `red_yellow_green`
    - Sequential: `green`, `blue`, `purple`, `orange`, `gray`
    - Backward-compatible aliases: `red_white_green` → `red_green`
  </conditional_formatting_types>
</options>

<examples>
  <columns_full>
    ```yaml
    columns:
      # Dimension — pinned, with mapping
      - id: language
        label: Lang
        type: dimension
        width: { type: auto }
        pinned: left
        mapping: { id: languages }

      # Metric — aggregated, formatted
      - id: costs
        label: Costs
        type: metric
        aggregate: sum
        format: { type: currency, decimals: 0 }
        description: "Total ad spend across all campaigns"

      # Calculated — expression with NULLIF guard
      - id: roi_net
        label: ROI Net
        type: calculated
        expression: "(SUM(revenue_net) - SUM(costs)) / NULLIF(SUM(costs), 0) * 100"
        format: { type: percent, decimals: 1, suffix: "%" }

      # Timestamp column
      - id: updated_at
        label: Last Updated
        type: dimension
        format: { type: timestamp, pattern: "yyyy-MM-dd HH:mm" }
    ```
  </columns_full>

  <data_presets>
    ```yaml
    - id: campaign_table
      type: rich_table
      datasource: campaign_table__default_view
      data_presets:
        default_preset: high_roi              # Optional. Start with this preset
        on_apply:                             # Optional
          clear_user_filters: true
          clear_sorting: true
          clear_search: true
        presets:
          - id: dlo
            label: DLO
            sql: >
              SELECT * FROM {{source:__default_view}}
              WHERE lower(language) = 'dlo'
              ORDER BY costs DESC
          - id: high_roi
            label: High ROI
            description: Positive ROI campaigns
            projection: campaign_table__view_high_roi
            sorting: [{ id: roi, desc: true }]
    ```

    - `{{source:__default_view}}` resolves to widget datasource
    - UI: `[All] [DLO] [High ROI]` — "All" is widget datasource
    - Smart search index rebuilds automatically on preset switch
  </data_presets>

  <grouping>
    ```yaml
    grouping:
      enabled: true
      levels: [language, media_source, campaign]
      subtotal_levels: [[language, media_source]]
      default_expanded: false
      sticky:
        active_group_headers: true
        subtotals_under_grand: true
    ```
  </grouping>

  <pivot>
    ```yaml
    pivot:
      rows:
        - id: plan_name
          label: Type
        - id: payment_source
          label: Payment source
      columns:
        - id: day
          label: Day
          type: date
          desc: true
      values:
        - id: revenue_net
          label: Revenue
          aggregate: sum
          format: { type: currency, decimals: 0 }
      totals: { row: true, column: true }
      grand_total_label: "Total"
    ```

    Define `columns` for static row dimensions + `grand_total` metric:
    ```yaml
    columns:
      - id: plan_name
        label: Type
        type: dimension
        pinned: left
      - id: grand_total
        label: Total
        type: metric
        aggregate: sum
        format: { type: currency, decimals: 0 }
    ```
  </pivot>

  <filtering>
    ```yaml
    filtering:
      enabled: true
      show_filter_row: true
      global_search: true                    # Or expanded: { enabled: true, show_token_pills: false }
      columns:
        - { id: language, type: select, multi: true }
        - { id: media_source, type: select }
        - { id: campaign, type: text, match: contains }
        - { id: costs, type: number, operator: ">" }
        - { id: install_date, type: date, operator: between }
    ```

    Smart search tokens: `en` (keyword), `"hello world"` (quoted), `not nogti` (negation), `costs>300` (range).
  </filtering>

  <selectable_and_highlight>
    ```yaml
    # Source widget — selectable
    - id: campaigns_table
      type: rich_table
      selectable:
        multi: true
        select_all: true
        columns: [id, name, experiment_id]  # For consumer SQL refs

    # Consumer widget — highlight
    - id: details_table
      type: rich_table
      highlight:
        selection: campaigns_table
        column: campaign_id

    # Multiple highlight sources
    highlight:
      - selection: campaigns_table
        column: campaign_id
      - selection: countries_table
        column: country_code
    ```
    `selectable` and `highlight` are mutually exclusive on the same widget.
  </selectable_and_highlight>

  <selection_as_global_filter>
    Use `selectable.emit_filters` when a row selection must reach the BASE datasource
    SQL (not just a projection). Each entry (`{ filter_id, column }`) auto-injects a
    hidden, serializable global filter into the dashboard's `FilterProvider`, so the
    usual `${filters.<id>(...)}` macros resolve everywhere — in base datasources, in
    projections, and in other widgets.

    ```yaml
    # Base datasource references the (not-yet-declared) filter directly:
    datasources:
      ads:
        sql: |
          SELECT * FROM marts.spend
          WHERE ${filters.date_range('toDate(day)')}
            AND ${filters.selected_channel('channel').or_true}

    # Emitter table — selection drives the hidden filter:
    - id: channel-table
      type: rich_table
      datasource: by_channel
      filters:
        exclude: [selected_channel]   # self-scope: keep THIS table full
      selectable:
        multi: true
        emit_filters:
          - { filter_id: selected_channel, column: channel }
    ```

    Properties:
    - No manual `filters:` entry needed — the definition is synthesized.
    - Hidden from the chip bar, but still serializable → selection persists in URL
      and the matching rows are rehydrated on reload.
    - URL writes use `history.replaceState` so rapid row clicks do NOT pollute
      browser history (visible filters still use `pushState`).
    - `selectable.multi` controls single vs multi-valued filter.
    - Self-scoping: if the emitter table also consumes its own filter, set
      widget-level `filters.exclude: [<filter_id>]` — otherwise the driver view
      collapses to the selected row(s).

    When to use which:
    - `emit_filters` → cross-dashboard scope, affects base datasources.
    - `${selection.widget('col')}` → local master-detail inside a projection chain.
    - Both can coexist on the same selectable table.
  </selection_as_global_filter>

  <actions>
    Row actions have two distinct modes:
    - `href` opens a read-only navigation link and is available to dashboard readers.
    - `skill` runs a write skill and requires mutation access (`EXECUTE | WRITE`).

    Do not combine `href` and `skill` in the same action. Use `href` for external tools,
    admin pages, and drill-outs; use `skill` only for server-side mutations.
    For write-skill tables bound to projected data, prefer a named datasource projection with
    `materialized: true`; the client infers strict optimistic UPDATEs from the skill SQL and
    refreshes the projection locally. Do not add local SQL `post_actions` for standard table edits
    unless you are intentionally using a legacy fallback.

    ```yaml
    actions:
      open_lesson:
        label: Open Lesson
        icon: external-link
        quick: true
        href: "https://admin.example.com/courses/{course_id}/lessons/{lesson_id}"
        invalid_href: hide                   # default: hide | disabled | placeholder
      open_from_column:
        label: Open Resource
        icon: external-link
        href: "{resource_url}"               # full URL from row data
        when: "resource_url != ''"
      pause:
        label: Pause Campaign
        icon: pause
        quick: true                          # Show inline, not in dropdown
        when: "effective_status = 'ACTIVE'"  # Conditional visibility
        skill: pause_campaign                # Write skill datasource key
      archive:
        label: Archive Campaign
        icon: archive
        destructive: true                    # Confirmation dialog first
        skill: archive_campaign
    ```

    Link safety:
    - Placeholder values in path templates are URL-encoded.
    - Full URL placeholders like `{resource_url}` are decoded once and validated.
    - Invalid links are hidden by default. `invalid_href: disabled` shows a disabled
      action; `invalid_href: placeholder` shows a non-clickable invalid marker.
    - Dangerous schemes (`javascript:`, `data:`, `vbscript:`) are rejected by
      validation and blocked at runtime.
  </actions>

  <editable_columns>
    Editable columns should use a write skill whose final statement is a simple `UPDATE ... SET ... WHERE ...`.
    The optimistic path updates only columns explicitly present in the skill `SET` clause, then refreshes any
    dependent materialized projection before the server response settles.

    ```yaml
    - id: daily_budget
      label: Daily Budget
      type: metric
      aggregate: sum
      format: { type: currency, decimals: 2 }
      editable: true
      skill: update_campaign_budget
    ```
  </editable_columns>

  <column_tooltips>
    Three levels:

    **Level 1 — Auto:** Truncated headers show full label. No config needed.

    **Level 2 — Static:**
    ```yaml
    - id: ecpa
      label: eCPA
      type: calculated
      expression: "SUM(costs) / NULLIF(SUM(action), 0)"
      description: "Effective Cost Per Action."
    ```

    **Level 3 — Programmable:**
    ```yaml
    - id: roi
      label: ROI
      type: calculated
      description: Return on Investment
      tooltip:
        context:
          sql: |
            SELECT
              ROUND(AVG(roi_val), 1) as avg_roi,
              COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE roi_val > 0) as profitable,
              COUNT(*) as total
            FROM {{_self}}
        template: |
          **{{column.label}}**
          {{column.description}}
          ---
          Avg: {{context.avg_roi}}%
          Profitable: {{context.profitable}}/{{context.total}}
    ```
    `{{_self}}` resolves to current active datasource (respects data presets).
    Template vars: `{{column.id}}`, `{{column.label}}`, `{{column.description}}`, `{{context.*}}`.
  </column_tooltips>

  <conditional_formatting>
    ```yaml
    conditional_formatting:
      # Color scale with custom value_sql
      - column: roi
        type: color_scale
        palette: red_white_green
        apply_to: cell
        value_sql: |
          CASE
            WHEN costs > 2000 AND roi < 0 THEN -100
            WHEN roi >= 60 THEN 100
            ELSE roi
          END
        steps:
          - { value: -100, color: "#f3b3b3" }
          - { value: 0, color: "#f7f7f7" }
          - { value: 60, color: "#9cc3b0" }

      # Auto color scale — steps generated from data percentiles
      - column: revenue
        type: color_scale
        palette: red_yellow_green
        steps: auto

      # Auto color scale with sequential palette
      - column: score
        type: color_scale
        palette: blue
        steps: auto

      # Icon set
      - column: status
        type: icon_set
        rules:
          - { op: ">=", value: 80, icon: CheckCircle }
          - { op: ">=", value: 50, icon: AlertTriangle }
          - { op: "<", value: 50, icon: XCircle }

      # Data bar
      - column: costs
        type: data_bar
        min: 0
        max: 10000
        color: "#3b82f6"
    ```
  </conditional_formatting>

  <visualization>
    ```yaml
    visualization:
      density: compact
      row_height: medium
      zebra: true
      zebra_rows: odd
      style: default
      style_switcher: true
      abbreviate_numbers:
        rows: true
        subtotals: true
        totals: false
    ```
  </visualization>

  <export>
    CSV download enabled by default. Opt-out with `export: { enabled: false }`.

    ```yaml
    export:
      enabled: true
      formats: [csv]
      include_group_rows: false
      include_subtotals: false
    ```
  </export>

  <sorting>
    ```yaml
    sorting:
      enabled: true
      multi: true
      default:
        - { id: costs, desc: true }
    ```
  </sorting>

  <totals>
    ```yaml
    totals:
      enabled: true                          # Default: true
      sticky: bottom                         # true (top) | 'bottom' (default) | false
      label: "Total"
    ```
  </totals>

  <layout_presets>
    ```yaml
    layout:
      default_preset: comfortable
      show_reset: false
      presets:
        - id: compact
          label: Compact
          density: compact
          row_height: small
          columns:
            - id: campaign
              width: { type: flex, value: 2, min: 180, max: 420 }
        - id: comfortable
          label: Comfortable
          density: comfortable
          row_height: large
      responsive:
        - max_width: 1024
          preset: compact
    ```
  </layout_presets>
</examples>

<layout>
  <wide_tables>
    Use `col_span: 15` for wide tables with horizontal scroll.
  </wide_tables>

  <side_by_side_tables>
    Use section `layout: horizontal` + `columns: 2` for side-by-side tables:

    ```yaml
    sections:
      - id: comparison
        layout: horizontal
        columns: 2
        widgets:
          - id: left-table
            type: rich_table
            datasource: source_a
            columns: [...]
          - id: right-table
            type: rich_table
            datasource: source_b
            columns: [...]
    ```
  </side_by_side_tables>
</layout>

<patterns>
  <selection_sql>
    Consumer widgets reference selections in projection SQL:

    | Template | Selected | Empty |
    |---|---|---|
    | `${selection.widget('col')}` | `AND col IN ('a','b')` | `AND 1=1` |
    | `${selection.widget('col').if_set}` | `AND col IN (...)` | `` (empty) |
    | `${selection.widget('col').value}` | `'first_val'` | `NULL` |
    | `${selection.widget('col').values}` | `'a', 'b'` | `` (empty) |
  </selection_sql>

  <row_shimmer>
    During write skill execution: pulse animation, all actions disabled, editable cells read-only.
    After success: source invalidated, background re-fetch, fresh data loaded.
  </row_shimmer>
</patterns>

<rules>
  <hard_constraints>
    - `selectable` and `highlight` are mutually exclusive on the same widget
    - Export is enabled by default — opt-out with `export: { enabled: false }`
    - Totals use column `aggregate` if specified, else SUM
    - `value_sql` in conditional formatting is optional — evaluated for `data` rows only
    - Smart search index rebuilds automatically when datasource changes (preset switch, filter)
    - Sorting precedence: user manual → preset sorting → projection `ORDER BY` → widget default
    - Always guard division by zero in calculated expressions: `NULLIF(denominator, 0)`
    - Column profiling runs in parallel with main query — provides auto-decimals, percentiles, null/zero ratios, cardinality
    - `auto_hide: true` on a column enables auto-hiding when 100% of values are null (disabled by default)
    - `steps: auto` in `color_scale` generates gradient from data percentiles (min → P25 → P50 → P75 → max)
    - `palette` in `color_scale` accepts design-system names: `red_green`, `blue_orange`, `purple_teal`, `red_yellow_green`, `green`, `blue`, `purple`, `orange`, `gray`
    - `decimals` priority: YAML config > auto-detected from data > type default (currency=2, number=0, percent=0)
  </hard_constraints>

  <keyboard_navigation>
    Rich tables support full keyboard navigation when the table container has focus:

    | Key | Action |
    |-----|--------|
    | `↑` / `↓` | Move focus between rows |
    | `Enter` | Select / expand focused row |
    | `Space` | Toggle checkbox (when `selectable.multi` is enabled) |
    | `Home` / `End` | Jump to first / last row |
    | `Page Up` / `Page Down` | Jump by viewport height (adaptive to density) |
    | `s` | Focus SmartSearch input (when `global_search` is enabled) |

    ARIA attributes (`role="grid"`, `aria-activedescendant`) are set automatically.
    The focused row shows a visible focus ring using `--border-focus` from the design system.
    Virtual scroll keeps the focused row in the viewport via `scrollToIndex`.

    Keyboard navigation requires no YAML configuration — it is always available.
    The `s` shortcut only activates when `filtering.global_search` is enabled on the widget.
  </keyboard_navigation>
</rules>

